# CLAUDE.local.md

Template. Copy to `CLAUDE.local.md` and fill in — that file is git-ignored and
holds everything specific to one machine. `CLAUDE.md` stays portable.

    cp CLAUDE.local.md.example CLAUDE.local.md

## This install

- **Mods directory (this repo):** `<path>`
  - Recommended: `<standalone-install>/mods` — a copy of the game kept for development only
  - Otherwise: Windows `%APPDATA%\Factorio\mods` · macOS `~/Library/Application Support/factorio/mods` · Linux `~/.factorio/mods`
- **Game install:** `<path>`
  - Standalone (zip): the folder holding `bin/`, `data/` and `doc-html/` — one level above this repo
  - Windows (Steam) `C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Factorio`
  - macOS `/Applications/factorio.app/Contents` · Linux (Steam) `~/.steam/steam/steamapps/common/Factorio`
- **Factorio version:** `<e.g. base 2.1.12>` — read it from `<install>/data/base/info.json`
- **Expansions installed:** `<space-age, quality, elevated-rails, …>`
- **User-data folder:** `<path>` — holds `factorio-current.log` and `script-output/`.
  For a standalone install this is the **install root**, i.e. one level above this repo, because
  `config-path.cfg` carries `use-system-read-write-data-directories=false`. For Steam and the
  installers it is the system location. Getting this wrong means reading a stale log and
  calling a failed run a pass.

A dedicated dev install is worth the disk: nobody's play mods mix with the deliverables, the
version stays pinned instead of updating mid-project, and a standalone build keeps its own
`.lock`, so validation and screenshot runs work whatever else is running. `validate.ps1` and
`shoot.ps1` both detect an install they are nested inside, so neither needs configuring — and
both refuse rather than falling back to some other install they happen to find.

### Installs this workspace may use

List every install that is fair game, and what each is for — the default, a stable-branch one
for backports, a base-only one for the no-expansion path.

**Anything not on that list is out of scope**, in particular any copy of the game used for
actually playing: never read, never written, never validated against. Say so explicitly here if
such a copy exists on this machine, so it is a closed question rather than a judgement call.

Headless validation, fully expanded for this machine:

```
<install>/bin/x64/factorio --dump-data --mod-directory <isolated-dir>
```

## Git identity

Set locally in `.git/config` — never `--global`:

```
user.name  = <name>
user.email =
```

Remote is `origin` → `<url>`.

Leave `user.email` empty unless something needs an address: git accepts it and
commits are authored `<name> <>`, publishing nothing. Where an address is
required, use the forge's `<username>@users.noreply.<forge>` form, which keeps
commits linked to the account without exposing a real one. Never a real address.

Default `author` for new mods: `<name>`. Default `homepage`: `<url>`.

## Tooling

- **fmtk** (`factoriomod-debug`) `<version>` — `npm install -g factoriomod-debug`
- **Node** `<version>` (fmtk requires ≥ 22.7.0)
- **Blender** `<version>`, if doing graphics work
- Anything else the agent should not have to probe for

## Mod portal API key

`<not configured | stored in the OS credential store | FACTORIO_UPLOAD_API_KEY>`

Created at https://factorio.com/profile by the account owner — an agent cannot.
**Never write the key itself into this file.**

## Local-only folders

Git-ignored, so not in a fresh clone. Group by `CLAUDE.md` -> Folder classes, because
**git-ignored does not mean hands-off** — two of the classes are edited routinely, and the
class is what decides. `.claude/scripts/check-folder-scope.ps1` verifies this list against
what is actually on disk.

### Reference — read freely, never write

- **`exemples/`** — extracted reference mods, if built. See `CLAUDE.md` -> `exemples/`.

### Frozen vendor — do not read or modify unless asked

Each entry also needs `Edit(<folder>/**)` **and** `Write(<folder>/**)` deny rules in
`.claude/settings.json`.

- **`<third-party-mod-folder>/`** — unpacked mod from another author, present only so the game
  loads it. Note the author.

### Patched vendor — editable, never committed, never re-uploaded

- **`<forked-mod-folder>/`** — another author's mod, modified in place for a playthrough. Note
  the author and whether it ships a `LICENSE`; without one the source cannot be redistributed
  at all. Give it its own `CLAUDE.md` recording what was changed — with no baseline on disk,
  that file is the only history the edits have.

### Local mod — ours, editable, never published

- **`<local-mod-folder>/`** — our own mod that exists for one playthrough. Give it its own
  `CLAUDE.md`.

## Notes and scratch material

- `<paths to design notes, render logs, etc. kept outside the repo>`
